				<wikidot:authorName>Tutwater</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2855217</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>No disrespect to you or any of the involved authors (all dado SCPs that I've seen are at least alright to read, but then again I'm the guy that doesn't hate <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-952">SCP-952</a>), it's less dado or his products themselves and more the extent that this has reached.</p> <p>I'm frustrated that what (I feel like) <em>should</em> have been let alone as a single SCP or brief series now warrants its own hub page, when in my opinion the potential for creativity and innovation for this guy is really low and gets repetitive fast- he's close to getting the same recognition as your typical Group of Interest when I feel like the depth and intrigue is much much lesser</p> <p>I feel like a one-note joke is getting stretched to death for no reason besides <em>everything's got to be a GoI/canon/series now</em></p> <p>Maybe I don't see the joke for most articles besides &quot;dado writes in broken English&quot; and &quot;dado misunderstands what people say&quot;, and there's some subtext everyone else is getting out of it that I'm not? I don't know</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
